    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To complete the task, I need to create a Python file named `extract_receipt_fields.py` that uses a concrete external provider to extract specific fields from a receipt. I will use the Amazon Textract service, which is a powerful OCR service provided by AWS, to identify and extract text from documents. This will make the provider identifiable in the code through the use of the `boto3` library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, and the specific service client for Textract. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860538841,
          "start": 1789860535598
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc005d2e0017uVJqQsBMQefFn",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc0057a50015VQAvD4FOmYkD1",
